                <pb facs="0895" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1624a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-04T15:00:00-05:00">October 4, 1935—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>185. Would you telegraph whether in your opinion there is any probability of the
                    League Council tomorrow deciding that a state of war exists in Ethiopia. If you
                    consider it advisable, I would be glad to have you telephone the Department at
                    any time before noon, Washington Time, tomorrow, Saturday, October 5, that you
                    might be able to give us the latest developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
